{"status":"ready","content":"Let the sample be $x = \\{25, 10, 0, 9, -1, -14, -21\\}$.\nThe number of observations is $n = 7$.\n\nFirst, we compute the sample mean, $\\bar{x}$:\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{\\sum x_i}{n}$\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{25 + 10 + 0 + 9 + (-1) + (-14) + (-21)}{7}$\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{25 + 10 + 9 - 1 - 14 - 21}{7}$\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{44 - 36}{7}$\n$\\bar{x} = \\frac{8}{7}$\n\nNext, we compute the deviations from the mean, $(x_i - \\bar{x})$:\n$25 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{175 - 8}{7} = \\frac{167}{7}$\n$10 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{70 - 8}{7} = \\frac{62}{7}$\n$0 - \\frac{8}{7} = -\\frac{8}{7}$\n$9 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{63 - 8}{7} = \\frac{55}{7}$\n$-1 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{-7 - 8}{7} = -\\frac{15}{7}$\n$-14 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{-98 - 8}{7} = -\\frac{106}{7}$\n$-21 - \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{-147 - 8}{7} = -\\frac{155}{7}$\n\nNow, we square these deviations, $(x_i - \\bar{x})^2$:\n$(\\frac{167}{7})^2 = \\frac{27889}{49}$\n$(\\frac{62}{7})^2 = \\frac{3844}{49}$\n$(-\\frac{8}{7})^2 = \\frac{64}{49}$\n$(\\frac{55}{7})^2 = \\frac{3025}{49}$\n$(-\\frac{15}{7})^2 = \\frac{225}{49}$\n$(-\\frac{106}{7})^2 = \\frac{11236}{49}$\n$(-\\frac{155}{7})^2 = \\frac{24025}{49}$\n\nThen, we sum the squared deviations:\n$\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = \\frac{27889 + 3844 + 64 + 3025 + 225 + 11236 + 24025}{49}$\n$\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = \\frac{70308}{49}$\n\nNext, we compute the sample variance, $s^2$:\n$s^2 = \\frac{\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2}{n-1}$\n$s^2 = \\frac{\\frac{70308}{49}}{7-1}$\n$s^2 = \\frac{\\frac{70308}{49}}{6}$\n$s^2 = \\frac{70308}{49 \\times 6}$\n$s^2 = \\frac{70308}{294}$\n$s^2 = 239.142857...$\n\nAlternatively, we can use the formula $s^2 = \\frac{\\sum x_i^2 - \\frac{(\\sum x_i)^2}{n}}{n-1}$.\nFirst, calculate $\\sum x_i^2$:\n$25^2 = 625$\n$10^2 = 100$\n$0^2 = 0$\n$9^2 = 81$\n$(-1)^2 = 1$\n$(-14)^2 = 196$\n$(-21)^2 = 441$\n$\\sum x_i^2 = 625 + 100 + 0 + 81 + 1 + 196 + 441 = 1444$\nWe already computed $\\sum x_i = 8$.\n$(\\sum x_i)^2 = 8^2 = 64$.\n$\\frac{(\\sum x_i)^2}{n} = \\frac{64}{7}$.\n\n$s^2 = \\frac{1444 - \\frac{64}{7}}{7-1}$\n$s^2 = \\frac{\\frac{1444 \\times 7 - 64}{7}}{6}$\n$s^2 = \\frac{10108 - 64}{7 \\times 6}$\n$s^2 = \\frac{10044}{42}$\n$s^2 = 239.142857...$\n\nNow, we compute the sample standard deviation, $s$:\n$s = \\sqrt{s^2}$\n$s = \\sqrt{\\frac{10044}{42}}$\n$s = \\sqrt{\\frac{1674}{7}}$\n$s \\approx \\sqrt{239.142857...}$\n$s \\approx 15.464245$\n\nLet's double check the sum of squared deviations calculation to ensure no arithmetic errors.\n$\\bar{x} = 8/7$.\n$x_i$: 25, 10, 0, 9, -1, -14, -21\n$x_i - \\bar{x}$: $167/7$, $62/7$, $-8/7$, $55/7$, $-15/7$, $-106/7$, $-155/7$\n$(x_i - \\bar{x})^2$: $27889/49$, $3844/49$, $64/49$, $3025/49$, $225/49$, $11236/49$, $24025/49$\nSum of squared deviations numerator: $27889 + 3844 + 64 + 3025 + 225 + 11236 + 24025 = 70308$.\n$s^2 = \\frac{70308/49}{6} = \\frac{70308}{294} = \\frac{11718}{49}$.\nLet's recompute using the second formula:\n$\\sum x_i = 8$.\n$\\sum x_i^2 = 625+100+0+81+1+196+441 = 1444$.\n$s^2 = \\frac{1444 - \\frac{8^2}{7}}{7-1} = \\frac{1444 - \\frac{64}{7}}{6} = \\frac{\\frac{1444 \\times 7 - 64}{7}}{6} = \\frac{10108 - 64}{42} = \\frac{10044}{42} = \\frac{1674}{7}$.\n\nAh, there was a calculation error in the sum of squares.\n$s^2 = \\frac{1674}{7}$\n$s = \\sqrt{\\frac{1674}{7}} = \\sqrt{239.142857...} \\approx 15.464245$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{15.464}$.\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite","modelId":"google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite","promptId":"365-LiveBench-Math","request":{"maxOutputTokens":5000,"reasoning":{"effort":null,"exclude":null}},"response":{"id":"gen-1779368136-A0Uav0rircQ4CBwyNyWj","model":"google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite","finishReason":"stop","nativeFinishReason":"STOP","reasoningReturned":false},"usage":{"completion_tokens":1836,"prompt_tokens":43,"total_tokens":1879,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"image_